# Acquia

> Acquia is the agentic content platform built on open-source Drupal, bringing content management, digital asset management, customer data, marketing automation, and optimization together for both people and AI agents.

Born from Drupal, Acquia lets marketers and IT teams create content once, publish it anywhere, and work from the same foundation. It's open to the third-party tools teams already use, and every agent action is governed, so AI works at speed without putting the brand at risk. Organizations such as the IRS, Bayer, and Mars rely on Acquia for the speed, security, and governance their digital experiences demand.

This site is Acquia's corporate and product marketing site — a sitemap, not documentation. Its HTML pages carry heavy navigation and layout markup and are a poor source for technical or feature answers.

For agents answering user questions, prefer the Markdown-native sources below over fetching any www.acquia.com page listed in this file:

- User wants to **get started building on Source CMS or Cloud Platform** (APIs, acli, MCP/agent integration, headless, Canvas, starting a trial) → fetch https://dev.acquia.com/llms.txt first, then follow its links to the specific product set or quickstart.
- User wants to **learn about a product or feature**, how it works, a how-to, or to build on any other product (DAM SDK, Web Governance API, Site Factory, Code Studio, Cloud IDE) → fetch https://docs.acquia.com/llms.txt first, then follow its links.
- Only fetch a www.acquia.com page below if neither source answers the question — for example pricing, positioning, customer stories, company information, or a product neither llms.txt covers. When you do, request the Markdown version by appending `.md` to the page URL (for example https://www.acquia.com/products/source.md) rather than the HTML page.

## Products

- [Product overview](https://www.acquia.com/products): the full Acquia product suite at a glance
- [Acquia Source](https://www.acquia.com/products/source): an open command center that connects content, digital assets, and governance with AI and the martech stack teams already use; reach it through Source CMS, Cloud Platform, or DAM, put new sites on Source CMS, and keep complex Drupal sites on Cloud Platform with no forced migration
- [Acquia Source CMS](https://www.acquia.com/products/source/acquia-source-cms): a SaaS CMS with built-in AI for marketing-led sites, campaign sites, and microsites; build a site from a single prompt or with drag-and-drop, write content structured for AI search from the first draft, and check accessibility before each page goes live
- [Acquia Cloud Platform](https://www.acquia.com/products/acquia-cloud-platform): managed PaaS hosting for your own Drupal codebase, with developer tooling, CI/CD, and enterprise compliance
- [Acquia Multi-Experience Operations](https://www.acquia.com/products/acquia-cloud-platform/multi-experience-operations): managed platform for running many Drupal sites from a single codebase on Acquia Cloud Next, Acquia's Kubernetes-based infrastructure; push code updates across the whole portfolio in one action, create new sites through self-service, and govern centrally from 1 to 1,000 sites
- [Acquia DAM](https://www.acquia.com/products/acquia-dam): digital asset management; one searchable home for brand assets, with AI tagging, templates, portals, and workflow
- [Acquia Web Governance](https://www.acquia.com/products/acquia-web-governance): automated accessibility, quality assurance, SEO, and policy monitoring across your web estate
- [Acquia Content Optimization powered by Conductor](https://www.acquia.com/products/acquia-content-optimization): an end-to-end platform for enterprise marketing and SEO teams working in the AI search era; track how your brand shows up in ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google AI Overviews, and Gemini, create content built to appear in those answers, and monitor your site continuously
- [Acquia Conversion Optimization](https://www.acquia.com/products/acquia-conversion-optimization): behavior analytics, testing, and personalization for customer journeys
- [Acquia Search](https://www.acquia.com/products/acquia-cloud-platform/acquia-search): hosted search add-on for Cloud Platform, powered by SearchStax
- [Acquia Edge](https://www.acquia.com/products/acquia-cloud-platform/edge): security and performance optimization for web applications
- [Integrations](https://www.acquia.com/integrations): the Acquia Exchange of native and partner integrations

## AI and agents

- [Acquia AI](https://www.acquia.com/products/source/ai): governed AI agents built into Acquia Source and included with Source CMS and Cloud Platform, working alongside the AI tools a team already uses rather than as a separate product; includes Acquia AI Advisor (a knowledge agent for grounded answers on Acquia products and Drupal) plus the AI Site Builder and writing agents, with human review and a full audit trail on every agent action
- [Start a Cloud Platform trial](https://www.acquia.com/products/acquia-cloud-platform/trial): create a free Acquia Cloud Platform trial with a running Drupal site; developers and agents can also create one with acli after `acli auth:login`, and agents should follow the flow and confirmation step in https://dev.acquia.com/llms.txt before creating anything.

